y dent the margin, not the outcome"], "rationale": "Every recent likely-voter poll puts Becerra ahead by at least 18 points in a state that leans 12 points Democratic, and all seven raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic. Hilton's fundraising edge and affordability messaging have not moved the numbers, so the race is a Safe Democratic hold despite Becerra's lukewarm personal ratings.", "watch": "A strong debate performance by Hilton or fresh evidence of Democratic voter apathy could narrow the margin, though a genuine upset would require a historic shift.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gavin Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's open governor's race pits Democrat Xavier Becerra against Republican Steve Hilton, with the state's D+12 partisan lean framing the contest. Every major rating outfit calls the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and September polls of likely voters uniformly show Becerra ahead by roughly 18 to 25 points, including surveys from Berkeley IGS, PPIC, and SurveyUSA. Prediction markets price Becerra's chances near 96 percent.\n\nHilton has slightly outraised Becerra and has campaigned on an affordability agenda, while coverage notes lagging enthusiasm and softer voter views of Becerra, whose low-profile strategy has drawn criticism. Still, no public poll has shown the race within single digits, and Democrats' structural advantage in statewide California contests has held steady all cycle. The main open question is the size of Becerra's winning margin rather than who wins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem":